;This file contains tables required by FEQ if detention
; ponds are being simulated. 

; Table# 10000 is based on work done for Du Page County
; by Tom Price of NIPC.  This table gives the number of
; acre-feet/acre of detention storage required
;  for each level of imperviousnes and allowed release
; rate in ft^3/sec/acre.  The values in this table are
; used to determine the detention pond volume given
; a release rate, and the level of imperviousnous defined
; in the TRIBUTARY-AREA input block for the detenion
; basin. 

TABLE#=10000
TYPE=   10
LABEL= Unit area detention volume function
; left hand column contains impervious fraction
; top row contains the release rate
impfrc  0.05  0.10  0.20  0.30
  0.00 0.266 0.245 0.210 0.185
  0.25 0.353 0.330 0.288 0.255
  0.50 0.441 0.393 0.335 0.301
  0.75 0.534 0.468 0.398 0.362
  1.00 0.638 0.554 0.467 0.429
  -1.0


; Table 10001 gives the orifice function defining
; both weir and orifice flow through a circular 
; orifice.  The table is in dimensionless form
; so that it applies to all units of measure and
; to all sizes of orifices within the typical
; limits of meaningful flow.  See Bos and the
; FEQUTL documention for more details.  Reference
; to Bos is in the FEQUTL document. 

