; Table 10002 gives the only approximation to the relationship between 
; total impervious area and the directly connected or hydrologically
; significant impervious area that I could find.  It is based on a figure appearing for
; many years with the SWM, HSP, HSPX, and HSPF.  Its origin is unknown.
; The only two points that are known exactly are those at 0.0 
; fraction of area and those at 1.0 fraction of area.  Between these
; two extremes the directly connected impervious area will be less than
; or equal to the total impervious area.  This table is for approximate
; purposes.  It is only used to convert the directly connected impervious
; area in the tributary area input for FEQ to the total impervious
; area that is used in the lagtime equations. 
TABLE#=10002
TYPE=   -2
REFL=0.0
 DrImpArea TtImpArea
       0.0       0.0
     0.125      0.25
      0.34      0.50
     0.635      0.75
     1.00       1.00
    -1.0 